  "generated_text": "To find the residue of $-811\\pmod{24}$, we need to find the remainder when $-811$ is divided by $24$.\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when $811$ is divided by $24$:\n\\[ 811 \\div 24 = 33 \\text{ remainder } 19 \\]\nSo, $811 \\equiv 19 \\pmod{24}$.\n\nSince $-811 \\equiv -19 \\pmod{24}$, we need to find the remainder when $-19$ is divided by $24$:\n\\[ -19 \\div 24 = -1 \\text{ remainder } 35 \\]\nSo, $-19 \\equiv 35 \\pmod{24}$.\n\nHowever, we need the residue to be in the range $0$ to $23$. Therefore, we subtract $24$ from $35$:\n\\[ 35 - 24 = 11 \\]\n\nThus, the residue of $-811\\pmod{24}$ is $\\boxed{11}$.",
